# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository for every text file. No
# tracked file is CRLF today, so this renormalizes nothing; it keeps it that way.
* text=auto

# Pin LF in the WORKING TREE too, whatever the host's core.autocrlf says. The
# load-bearing case is the justfile: CI runs `just test-fast` on windows-latest,
# where a default checkout is CRLF. The shell scripts only ever execute inside
# the Linux test container, but a CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line breaks the
# interpreter lookup, so they get the same pin rather than relying on luck.
*.sh text eol=lf
justfile text eol=lf
